      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Stabilize one video segment and persist its motion matrix.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --seg-id TEXT REQUIRED \r\n                              Target video segment id (raw id, no seg_id= prefix)\r\n          --timeout <duration> \r\n                              Execution timeout; explicit unit required, e.g. 5min or 300s\r\n          --level TEXT        Stabilization level: recommended (balanced stability/crop,\r\n                              default), minimum-crop (least crop), or most-stable (strongest\r\n                              stabilization)\r\n          --disable           Disable video stabilization on the target segment\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Apply the default recommended level: balanced stability and crop\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo video-stabilize --seg-id <VIDEO_UUID>\r\n  # Prefer less crop, with weaker stabilization\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo video-stabilize --level minimum-crop \\\r\n      --seg-id <VIDEO_UUID>\r\n  # Prefer the strongest stabilization, which may crop more\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo video-stabilize --level most-stable \\\r\n      --seg-id <VIDEO_UUID>\r\n  # Turn video stabilization off\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo video-stabilize --disable --seg-id <VIDEO_UUID>\r\n\r\nNOTES\r\n  - --level values align with the app UI: recommended, minimum-crop, most-stable.\r\n  - The command waits for 